# Files the Vercel CLI must not upload as part of a deployment.
#
# 🔴 Why this file has to exist at all: `.claude/` is already in .gitignore, but
# the CLI still offered its contents to the API — each Claude Code worktree under
# .claude/worktrees/ is its OWN git checkout, and a nested .git defeats the root
# .gitignore walk. With ten worktrees present that turned a 3.1k-file repository
# into a 31,010-file upload and the deploy failed outright:
#
#   Invalid request: `files` should NOT have more than 15000 items, received 31010.
#
# So the deploy's file count scaled with how many sibling sessions happened to
# have worktrees on disk — nothing to do with the commit being shipped.
#
# Note this does NOT re-expose node_modules/.git/.next/.env.local: the CLI
# excludes those unconditionally, independent of this file
# (https://vercel.com/docs/builds/build-features → default ignored files).
# Keep entries here to things that genuinely must never ship.

.claude/
